1
00:00:04,250 --> 00:00:06,370
Fit once, and use it everywhere.

2
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:17,695
The last film ran many requests as one. Now they share a model. A fits entry is an ordinary request with one regression, and it runs once, before any slot.

3
00:00:18,495 --> 00:00:27,868
On film seventeen's cohort, with the true decays written in, the fit recovers both slopes. Its full result comes back under fits, keyed by name.

4
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:36,505
Each slot scores its own rows with a regression predict attribute: the same model, scored at full precision, never refitted.

5
00:00:37,305 --> 00:00:44,566
A formula or a filter reads one figure with coef: here, TV's slope times its adstock, summed per market.

6
00:00:45,366 --> 00:00:51,582
Fits share one namespace. A misspelt name is refused, and the error lists the names that are bound.

7
00:00:52,382 --> 00:01:00,433
Predict lists every fit without fitting it, and judges every name and kind first. A fit that fails on its data fails alone.

8
00:01:01,233 --> 00:01:09,156
Now film seventeen's search, with one entry more. From sweep names the sweep body's regression, instead of writing a request.

9
00:01:09,956 --> 00:01:17,815
The same seed gives the same winner, slot thirty-nine. Pulse refits its regression on that slot's rows, under the name best.

10
00:01:18,615 --> 00:01:26,218
The bound fit matches the winning slot figure for figure. With no winner, it carries an error. There is no fallback to rank two.

11
00:01:27,018 --> 00:01:34,621
A batch with a binding runs sweep-first: the sweep slots, the rank, the bound fit, then optimize and the explicit slots.

12
00:01:35,421 --> 00:01:42,981
Sweep axis reads the winner's decay as a number. Here it turns into a steady-state multiplier, with no label parsing.

13
00:01:43,781 --> 00:01:52,045
TV's long-run effect lands close to the truth. Search's is nearly half too high: the weak channel film seventeen warned about.

14
00:01:52,845 --> 00:01:57,824
A bound fit is one slot's answer. Read the top few ranks before you trust it.

15
00:01:58,624 --> 00:02:07,251
The sweep may vary the data, never the model: type, target and predictors match in every slot, so predict can check names with no data.

16
00:02:08,051 --> 00:02:16,571
Remove the rank and nothing can win, so the batch is refused before it runs. A slot that reads the fit it feeds is refused too.

17
00:02:17,371 --> 00:02:23,864
Otherwise a bound fit is an ordinary fit: read it with coef, score it, optimize over it, save it.

18
00:02:24,664 --> 00:02:31,499
For a media mix we need returns that bend. A sibling cohort keeps the same spend, but its sales saturate.

19
00:02:32,299 --> 00:02:42,440
The Hill media-mix regression fits every channel's slope and Hill curve together: k is the half-saturation point, s the shape. It reads adstocks built upstream.

20
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:47,685
Here are the fitted curves. TV keeps climbing; search flattens fast.

21
00:02:48,485 --> 00:02:56,088
The whole workflow is one Compose call. A Latin hypercube sweep searches both decays, each slot fitting the Hill model.

22
00:02:56,888 --> 00:02:59,520
A from sweep fit binds the winner and saves it.

23
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:06,579
A contribution slot rebuilds each adstock at the winning decay, and an optimize block splits the budget.

24
00:03:07,379 --> 00:03:13,808
Budget and caps are your own figures, passed as params. The sweep's samples count against the slot limit.

25
00:03:14,608 --> 00:03:21,891
The near-best ranks agree on TV: about point six, its true decay. On search they sit near point five five.

26
00:03:22,691 --> 00:03:30,464
The fit reports betas, then each channel's k and s. Search's shape sits on its upper bound, so its standard error is null.

27
00:03:31,264 --> 00:03:38,803
Search's true decay was point two. Report the spread across near-best ranks, and treat a parameter on a bound as a warning.

28
00:03:39,603 --> 00:03:47,931
A window's decay is written in the request, so the slot rebuilds the adstock: fanned-out lags, and a formula applying the winning decay.

29
00:03:48,731 --> 00:03:54,563
Then each channel's contribution is its fitted slope times its curve, read with coef and hill.

30
00:03:55,363 --> 00:04:01,984
Summed per market, TV carries 28 to 32 percent of sales, and search 11 to 12 percent.

31
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:12,456
An optimize block maximises an expression over bounded variables, under constraints. Here, the steady-state curves, with spend summing to the budget.

32
00:04:13,256 --> 00:04:23,803
Multi-start S L S Q P finds TV at twenty-one and search at its cap of twelve. Only three of eight starts agree, so raise starts before you trust it.

33
00:04:24,603 --> 00:04:31,950
On these curves, the current mix makes about a hundred and forty-eight a week. The optimum makes a hundred and sixty-two.

34
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:41,675
Each variable's marginal is the gain from one more unit. The budget's multiplier is the shadow price: what one more unit of budget adds.

35
00:04:42,475 --> 00:04:49,480
At the optimum, TV, which is free, earns exactly the multiplier. Search, held at its cap, earns more.

36
00:04:50,280 --> 00:05:00,059
That is the reading: free channels equalise marginal ROI. A channel above it wants a higher cap; one below it, at zero, is not worth a unit.

37
00:05:00,859 --> 00:05:08,419
A budget the bounds cannot reach is infeasible. That block fails alone, with a slot-failed warning, and the rest survives.

38
00:05:09,219 --> 00:05:13,814
Save writes the fit under the data root as a model file, at full precision.

39
00:05:14,614 --> 00:05:21,491
A later request loads it under models and scores with no refit. Here it tracks average sales in both years.

40
00:05:22,291 --> 00:05:30,811
A vector fit saves as a population. Loaded under populations, it scores another year's weeks by their distance from twenty twenty-four.

41
00:05:31,611 --> 00:05:41,816
The Bayesian media-mix regression takes raw spend and adstocks it inside the model, so each decay gets its own posterior. It fits one market at a time.

42
00:05:42,616 --> 00:05:51,669
Check the diagnostics first. At the default, some transitions diverged. That is reported, not refused. Raising target accept cleared it.

43
00:05:52,469 --> 00:06:00,861
Its intervals cover both true decays, search's included. Search's R O I interval is wide: read its width, not its centre.

44
00:06:01,661 --> 00:06:08,432
It cannot save, score or optimize. Use the sweep to allocate budget, and Bayes to say how sure you are.

45
00:06:09,232 --> 00:06:16,259
That's Compose today: fits that run once, a bound winner, media-mix curves, an optimizer, and models you keep.

46
00:06:17,059 --> 00:06:26,752
More are added over time, and the manifest lists what your instance offers. Embedders can register their own regressions through options dot extensions.

47
00:06:27,552 --> 00:06:32,296
Batches, sweeps and banners were the last film. Next, derived cohorts.

48
00:06:33,096 --> 00:06:34,363
Pulse Compose.
